.TH STMKDISK 1 "2026-10-17" "stcc 0.4.0"
.SH NAME
stmkdisk \- create an Atari FAT12 floppy image for Hatari and Steem Engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stmkdisk
.BI \-o " IMAGE.ST"
.RI [ options ] " [FILE|DIRECTORY ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a raw .ST floppy image, default 720 KiB, from regular files and recursive
directories. No mount, root privileges, external filesystem tools or ROM are
needed to create an image. TOS or EmuTOS is needed to use it in an emulator.
Image names use uppercase ASCII 8.3. Long names must be explicitly mapped.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " IMAGE.ST"
Required output path. Existing images are refused unless --force is given.
.TP
.BI \-\-size " 360|720|800"
Capacity in KiB. All use 80 tracks, 512-byte sectors, and FAT12 with 1 KiB clusters.
360 KiB has one side; 720 and 800 KiB have two. 800 KiB uses 10 sectors/track.
.TP
.BI \-\-label " LABEL"
Volume label, 1 to 11 ASCII characters. Default STCC.
.TP
.BI \-\-root " DIRECTORY"
Import directory contents into the root, without the directory's own name.
.TP
.BI \-\-add " SOURCE DEST"
Import under an explicit relative 8.3 path. Create missing destination parents.
.TP
.BI \-\-auto " PROGRAM"
Copy an 8.3 .PRG or .TOS file to AUTO, using .PRG in the image.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Replace an existing output image after all input validation succeeds.
.TP
.B \-\-
Treat following arguments as source paths.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
stcc hello.c -o HELLO.TOS
stmkdisk -o DEMO.ST --auto HELLO.TOS --add readme.txt LIREMOI.TXT
hatari --tos /path/etos192us.img --disk-a DEMO.ST
.fi
.SH NOTES
Symlinks, special files, duplicate names, root directory overflow and disk full
are rejected. Timestamps are fixed and the Atari media serial is content-derived.
The boot sector is non-executable; AUTO startup is handled by TOS.
Without inputs, an empty formatted image is created. Publication without --force
requires a filesystem supporting POSIX hard links.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success; nonzero with a diagnostic on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stcc (1)
and MKDISK.md in the installed stcc documentation directory.
